<mxfile><diagram id="module-gem-box" name="Page-1"><mxGraphModel dx="0" dy="0" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="717" pageHeight="233" math="1" shadow="0"><root><mxCell id="0"/><mxCell id="1" parent="0"/><mxCell id="11" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 9.7px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;gene tokens&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;\(h_g\) from the backbone, perturbed graph" style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=8.3;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#666666;strokeWidth=0.8;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=3;spacingLeft=4;spacingRight=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0.00" y="0.00" width="62.00" height="88.00" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="12" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 9.7px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;availability gate&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;\(\gamma_g=\sigma(w^{\top}h_g)\); a deleted gene is set to 0 hard; no abundance head" style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=8.3;fillColor=#FFE6CC;strokeColor=#D79B00;strokeWidth=1.8;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=3;spacingLeft=4;spacingRight=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="75.00" y="0.00" width="96.00" height="88.00" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="13" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 9.7px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;GPR fold&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;reaction availability \(c_j\): softmin over a complex's subunits, sum over isozymes" style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=8.3;fillColor=#FFF2CC;strokeColor=#D6B656;strokeWidth=0.8;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=3;spacingLeft=4;spacingRight=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="184.00" y="0.00" width="84.00" height="88.00" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="14" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 9.7px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;box&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;\([\ell_j c_j,\ u_j c_j]\), the GEM's own bounds scaled by availability; no \(k_{\mathrm{cat}}\) ceiling, no second law" style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=8.3;fillColor=#FFF2CC;strokeColor=#D6B656;strokeWidth=1.8;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=3;spacingLeft=4;spacingRight=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="281.00" y="0.00" width="96.00" height="88.00" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="15" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 9.7px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;growth LP&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;\(\max\ v_{\mathrm{growth}}\) s.t. \(Sv=0,\ \ell c\le v\le uc\)&lt;br&gt;HiGHS per genotype; from round 27 a solved program is stored and reused when its bounds carry no gradient" style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=8.3;fillColor=#FFF2CC;strokeColor=#D6B656;strokeWidth=0.8;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=3;spacingLeft=4;spacingRight=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="390.00" y="0.00" width="130.00" height="88.00" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="16" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 9.7px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;optimum&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;\(v^*\), \(z^*\)" style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=8.3;fillColor=#FFF2CC;strokeColor=#D6B656;strokeWidth=0.8;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=3;spacingLeft=4;spacingRight=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="533.00" y="0.00" width="44.00" height="88.00" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="17" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 9.7px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;readout&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;round 15b, gated: \(\ell=\mathrm{head}(z)+g\,(a\,z^*+b)\)&lt;br&gt;rounds 24 and 27: \(+\,w^{\top}\log(1+|v^*|),\ w_0=0\)" style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=8.3;fillColor=#F8CECC;strokeColor=#B85450;strokeWidth=0.8;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=3;spacingLeft=4;spacingRight=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="590.00" y="0.00" width="127.00" height="88.00" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="18" value="" style="endArrow=blockThin;endFill=1;endSize=5;html=1;strokeColor=#000000;strokeWidth=0.8;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=8.3;labelBackgroundColor=#FFFFFF;" edge="1" parent="1" source="11" target="12"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="19" value="" style="endArrow=blockThin;endFill=1;endSize=5;html=1;strokeColor=#000000;strokeWidth=0.8;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=8.3;labelBackgroundColor=#FFFFFF;" edge="1" parent="1" source="12" target="13"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="20" value="" style="endArrow=blockThin;endFill=1;endSize=5;html=1;strokeColor=#000000;strokeWidth=0.8;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=8.3;labelBackgroundColor=#FFFFFF;" edge="1" parent="1" source="13" target="14"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="21" value="" style="endArrow=blockThin;endFill=1;endSize=5;html=1;strokeColor=#000000;strokeWidth=0.8;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=8.3;labelBackgroundColor=#FFFFFF;" edge="1" parent="1" source="14" target="15"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="22" value="" style="endArrow=blockThin;endFill=1;endSize=5;html=1;strokeColor=#000000;strokeWidth=0.8;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=8.3;labelBackgroundColor=#FFFFFF;" edge="1" parent="1" source="15" target="16"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="23" value="" style="endArrow=blockThin;endFill=1;endSize=5;html=1;strokeColor=#000000;strokeWidth=0.8;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=8.3;labelBackgroundColor=#FFFFFF;" edge="1" parent="1" source="16" target="17"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="24" value="" style="endArrow=blockThin;endFill=1;endSize=5;html=1;strokeColor=#000000;strokeWidth=0.8;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=8.3;labelBackgroundColor=#FFFFFF;dashed=1;dashPattern=4 3;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=1;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="15" target="12"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="455.00" y="114.00"/><mxPoint x="123.00" y="114.00"/></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="25" value="backward: \(\partial z^*/\partial u_j\) is the dual of the availability-scaled bound (envelope theorem), nonzero only where a gene-owned bound binds; through \(\gamma_g\) to the backbone" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=8.3;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;whiteSpace=wrap;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="133.00" y="118.00" width="312.00" height="24.00" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="26" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 9.7px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;by construction&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;\(Sv=0\) and \(\ell c\le v\le uc\) hold exactly at \(v^*\); the box is the GEM's, so it contains growth for every viable deletion&lt;br&gt;\(v^*\) enters the flux head detached, as a fixed feature of the current solve; only \(z^*\) carries a gradient&lt;br&gt;arm flux_off under the lp parameterization: no abundance head, no capacity ceiling, no thermodynamic term" style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=8.3;fillColor=#E1D5E7;strokeColor=#9673A6;strokeWidth=0.8;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=3;spacingLeft=4;spacingRight=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0.00" y="154.00" width="440.00" height="78.00" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="27" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 9.7px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;measured (rounds 15b, 24 and 27)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;round 15b: feasible from the first forward pass, the growth column ranks the held-out genes at 0.734 before training, and the forced cell receives no gradient when only exchange bounds bind; round 24: the flux head over this solve reads 0.852 on ProtT5; round 27: 0.882 on the pathway input, pooled 0.917" style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=8.3;fillColor=#F5F5F5;strokeColor=#666666;strokeWidth=0.8;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=3;spacingLeft=4;spacingRight=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="456.00" y="154.00" width="261.00" height="78.00" as="geometry"/></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram></mxfile>